WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.667
The enterprise multi-tenant AI platform.

2
00:00:03.967 --> 00:00:05.292
This is the capstone.

3
00:00:05.292 --> 00:00:09.900
It composes everything before it, and adds what enterprises actually buy.

4
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.600
Beyond the earlier blueprints, enterprises buy three things.

5
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.067
Isolation, so tenants never see each other's data.

6
00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:20.700
Governance, so every answer is traceable.

7
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.967
And cost attribution, so spend is tagged per tenant.

8
00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:27.567
Here is the request path, layer by layer.

9
00:00:27.867 --> 00:00:30.533
The gateway authenticates and tags the tenant.

10
00:00:30.833 --> 00:00:34.167
Retrieval is limited to that tenant's namespace and roles.

11
00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.167
Model routing picks the cheapest capable layer.

12
00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:41.267
Generation produces a cited answer from a versioned prompt.

13
00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:44.333
And an observability spine touches every layer.

14
00:00:45.533 --> 00:00:47.200
Now isolation in detail.

15
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.633
A query arrives tagged with its tenant.

16
00:00:49.933 --> 00:00:54.200
Retrieval can reach only that tenant's namespace, with RBAC enforced.

17
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.762
So the answer can only come from that tenant's documents.

18
00:00:57.762 --> 00:01:00.567
The model is never trusted to keep tenants apart.

19
00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:03.400
The spine feeds two payoffs.

20
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:08.367
Each trace records which documents, which model version and which prompt version.

21
00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:11.400
That becomes the audit log regulators ask for.

22
00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.733
Costs are tagged per tenant and feature at the gateway.

23
00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:18.333
So pricing and optimization are data, not guesses.

24
00:01:19.533 --> 00:01:21.233
Compare two interview answers.

25
00:01:21.533 --> 00:01:23.573
Weak: ask the model to behave.

26
00:01:23.573 --> 00:01:26.633
Winning: enforce isolation at the data layer.

27
00:01:26.933 --> 00:01:28.467
Weak: log some outputs.

28
00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:31.867
Winning: trace documents, model and prompt version.

29
00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.502
Weak: watch the bill.

30
00:01:33.502 --> 00:01:35.600
Winning: tag cost at the gateway.

31
00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:38.733
Deliver those three sentences and you win the room.

32
00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:40.678
Let's recap.

33
00:01:40.678 --> 00:01:43.533
This platform composes the earlier blueprints.

34
00:01:43.833 --> 00:01:46.900
Isolation lives in the data layer, not the prompt.

35
00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.767
Every answer is traceable.

36
00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:51.961
And cost is tagged per tenant at the gateway.

37
00:01:51.961 --> 00:01:54.533
Next up: system-design interview drills.
